==============================================================================
  THE BUS ROSTER IS THE RECORD'S. IT IS NOT THIS FILE'S.
==============================================================================
  This kernel holds a read seat on #registry.feed and replays it from its
  FIRST entry — at boot and at every look, never from a cursor. From that
  replay it derives every #channel node the record states, and:

    * it seats a bridge for each live one, on the spine stream the node
      binds, with no entry in kernel.toml and no restart;
    * the SURFACE HOST registers the matching frame-bus channel, because the
      registration capability lives in the process that embeds the bus and
      nowhere else, and it publishes every outcome it reaches;
    * an archive winds both down — the bridge seat here, the bus channel
      there, quiesced with the reason the record carries;
    * every registration this estate could NOT complete is a named
      divergence on the truth report, never a silence.

  What is still configuration, and can only be: the bootstrap set. The spine,
  the registry, the surface, and the bridge seats on genesis, registry.ops,
  registry.feed and manifold.kernel — every one of which must exist before a
  record can be read, the feed seat most of all.

  KERNEL-BRIEF R5 is implemented. Board #79 is closed.
==============================================================================
